From: =?UTF-8?q?L=C6=B0u=20Oa=20Oa?=
 <212658678+luuoaoa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 09:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Translate: keep the omnibox icon, kill the auto-popping
 bubble

The full-page Translate bubble auto-offering to translate foreign-language
pages is both annoying and a de-Google concern (the offer round-trips page
language to Google's translate infrastructure and nags on every visit). Kill
only the automatic offer while keeping the manual entry point intact.

The automatic "offer to translate this page" path routes through
TranslateManager::MaterializeDecision, which calls the client's
ShowTranslateUI() with the BEFORE_TRANSLATE step and triggered_from_menu ==
false. An explicit user gesture never reaches this method: clicking the
omnibox page-action icon dispatches IDC_SHOW_TRANSLATE, whose command handler
calls BrowserWindow::ShowTranslateBubble() directly with is_user_gesture ==
true. So suppressing BEFORE_TRANSLATE + !triggered_from_menu in
ChromeTranslateClient::ShowTranslateUI removes exactly the auto-pop and
nothing else.

The omnibox icon is unaffected: it is driven by
LanguageState::translate_enabled(), which TranslateManager::MaybeShowOmniboxIcon
sets unconditionally (translate_manager.cc) and which
TranslatePageActionController observes to show/hide the page action. That path
never consults the bubble, so the icon still lights up on translatable pages
and the user can click it to translate manually.
---
 .../browser/translate/chrome_translate_client.cc  | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/translate/chrome_translate_client.cc b/chrome/browser/translate/chrome_translate_client.cc
index 146610bc1c..7df49f2c63 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/translate/chrome_translate_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/translate/chrome_translate_client.cc
@@ -343,6 +343,21 @@ bool ChromeTranslateClient::ShowTranslateUI(
 #else
   DCHECK(TranslateService::IsTranslateBubbleEnabled());
   // Bubble UI.
+  // NOTE(colorburst fork): never let the full-page translate bubble pop up on
+  // its own. The automatic "offer to translate this page" path (see
+  // TranslateManager::MaterializeDecision) reaches here with the
+  // BEFORE_TRANSLATE step and triggered_from_menu==false; suppress it so the
+  // bubble only ever opens from an explicit user gesture -- the omnibox
+  // page-action icon routes through browser_commands' ShowTranslateBubble()
+  // with is_user_gesture==true and never enters this method, and menu-driven
+  // translation arrives with triggered_from_menu==true. The omnibox icon
+  // itself is driven separately by LanguageState::translate_enabled() (set in
+  // TranslateManager::MaybeShowOmniboxIcon) via TranslatePageActionController,
+  // so it still lights up on translatable pages for manual use.
+  if (step == translate::TRANSLATE_STEP_BEFORE_TRANSLATE &&
+      !triggered_from_menu) {
+    return false;
+  }
   if (step == translate::TRANSLATE_STEP_BEFORE_TRANSLATE &&
       translate_manager_->ShouldSuppressBubbleUI(target_language)) {
     return false;
